---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="lowland: Linux in your browser"
  description="Linux compiled for wasm32, with Web Workers as virtual CPUs and browser-provided virtio devices."
>
  <div slot="middle" class="root-header-info">
    <details open class="header-disclosure" data-persist-disclosure>
      <summary>how it works</summary>
      <div class="header-copy plain-copy">
        <p>
          Lowland runs a Linux kernel compiled for wasm32. Each virtual CPU runs in a Web Worker.
          JavaScript provides shared memory and virtio devices. No CPU emulator is involved.
        </p>
        <p>
          The terminal is connected to <code>/dev/hvc0</code> in the guest. Use the shell to inspect
          the system, run programs, or install packages with <code>apk</code>.
        </p>
        <p class="header-links">
          <a href="https://docs.low.land/getting-started/">browser tutorial →</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/tombl/linux">kernel source →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

  </div>

  <main class="root-stage">
    <h1 class="visually-hidden">Lowland Linux terminal</h1>
    <section class="machine" id="terminal" aria-label="Interactive Linux terminal">
      <pre class="terminal-placeholder" data-terminal-placeholder aria-live="polite">Loading Lowland Linux...
Fetching the kernel and root filesystem.

</pre>
      <div class="terminal" data-terminal aria-busy="true"></div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <script src="../scripts/site.ts"></script>
</Base>
